  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic partnership framework - SPF - 2022/23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SPF III framework is about sending out specialists to strengthen UN Women&#x2019;s capacity on national, regional and global level, and to assist with gender advisers to other entities. Outcome 1.1: More Women of all ages fully participate and lead in political processes and institutions. Integrated policy advice and high-level advocacy to advancing the normative agenda on women&#x2019;s participation in public life. Outcome 1.2 Gender responsive national laws, policies and budgets are developed and implemented at all levels by gender-responsive institutions. Outcome 3.1 More commitments on women, peace and security are implemented by Member States and the UN system, and more gender equality advocates influence peace and security processes.

Target groups are actors on global, regional, national and sub-national level. They are  female political candidates and peacebuilders, female leaders in all their variety, the most marginalised (incl. LGBTI+ persons, indigenous, young women, women with African background, migrants, women with disabilities, women with lower education and low income, women in rural areas), boys and men, member states and governments, including political institutions, parties, parliaments, peacebuilding institutions and Security Council.</narrative>
  </description>
